    "description": "<p>Kamiri are tall, narrow Scree with triangular heads, bright compound eyes and blade-like forearms. Their monasteries teach stillness, timing and the elimination of wasteful motion. Kamiri frequently become duellists, sword-masters and wandering judges.</p>\n<p>To a Kamiri, the perfect strike is not fast. It is simply made at the only moment in which it could succeed.</p>\n<p>You gain a +5 racial bonus to initiative checks and the Raptorial Blade natural attack:</p>\n<p><strong>Raptorial Blade</strong> – <strong>Dam</strong> 1d6 S; <strong>FDC</strong> 5; <strong>Traits</strong> Agile, Finesse, AR 1</p>\n<p><em>Granted:</em> a +5 racial bonus to Initiative, and the Raptorial Blade natural attack as a weapon.</p>",
